# What the sandbox makes when it runs, which is nobody's to commit.
#
# start.ps1 publishes each API into a folder of its own and points both of them
# at folders beside it for everything they write. All three are built from the
# submodules on demand: a clone of this repository and one run of the script
# makes them again.
#
#   game/     the game API, built, with a folder a day of logs under game/logs
#   chat/     the chat API, built, the same, and the rooms' own record beside
#   pics/     every picture a player puts up, kept apart from both services
#             because a face outlives any number of rebuilds of either
#
# Anchored to the root with the leading slash: unanchored, "game/" and "chat/"
# also matched DBScripts/game and DBScripts/chat, and kept every SQL script out
# of the repository.
/game/
/chat/
/pics/
COMMIT_MESSAGES.md